cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Cross Cell Evaluation of Electrochemical Impedance Features for Lithium Ion Battery Remaining Useful Life Prediction"
type: software
version: 3.0.2
date-released: 2026-09-25
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22964185"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sameredu/Battery-PIAI-ECM"
abstract: >-
  Evaluation of whether electrochemical impedance features transfer across
  lithium-ion cells. Electrolyte resistance Re and charge-transfer resistance
  Rct are read directly from the recorded impedance fields of the NASA
  Prognostics Center of Excellence dataset (B0005, B0006, B0007, B0018) with no
  circuit fitting. Between-cell variation is assessed with linear mixed-effects
  models because cycle-level measurements within a cell are strongly
  autocorrelated: the intraclass correlation is 0.899 for Re and 0.854 for Rct
  against 0.646 for capacity. A complete four-fold leave-one-battery-out random
  forest gives a mean RMSE of 19.05 cycles and a mean R-squared of 0.668, and a
  feature ablation shows this is carried by the capacity trajectory rather than
  by the impedance features. Impedance therefore discriminates strongly between
  nominally identical cells but transfers poorly as a predictor of remaining
  useful life.
keywords:
  - lithium-ion batteries
  - electrochemical impedance spectroscopy
  - remaining useful life
  - cross-cell validation
  - mixed-effects models
  - feature ablation
  - NASA battery dataset
